<br/>[h2 type=bar toc="Crafted Gear"]<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted &amp; Profession Gear for Discipline Priests</span></h2>Most crafted items aren't restricted by profession anymore, so even if you aren't a Tailor, you can still wear the Tailoring crafted items. There are a few exceptions to this, but we'll mention them below.<br/>
<br/>Most crafted items don't require you to have the profession anymore. We can wear Tailoring items, for example, even if we aren't Tailors. Note that there are some exceptions to this which we'll note below.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="phase-3-crafted-items-expensive-high-level">Phase 3 Crafted Items (Expensive, high level)</h4>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94280/falling-blossom-hood">
<img alt="Falling Blossom Hood" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cloth_raidpriest_m_01helm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Falling Blossom Hood</span></a> (requires materials from Throne of Thunder)</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94279/falling-blossom-sandals">
<img alt="Falling Blossom Sandals" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cloth_raidpriest_m_01boot.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Falling Blossom Sandals</span></a> (requires materials from Throne of Thunder)</div></li></ul>
