<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77533/lightweight-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Lightweight Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweight Retinal Armor</span></a> (Engineering only)</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> (Alchemy only). A strong pre-raid trinket that you can craft before you even hit max level!</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Discipline Priests</span></h2>Our <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=122098/divine-fury">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_sealofwrath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Divine Fury</span></a> passive gives us a 100% hit chance, which means you don't need to worry about getting Hit or Expertise.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Discipline Priests</span></h2>In Phase 1 we usually gemmed to maximize socket bonuses and intellect as priority. As the expansion goes on, pure secondary gems will rise in value relative to intellect gems since we get a lot more intellect and spell power on our gear. In Phase 3, characters that are early in the gearing process can continue the intellect-focused gem strategy but geared characters (520+ ilvl) can start swapping to pure secondary gems. <b>The difference between these two gem sets isn't very big.</b>
<br/>
<br/>Blue Sockets are by far our weakest, but most socket bonuses in Phase 3 are extremely good so you're usually going to include Purple or Green gems anyway.<br/>
<br/>
